#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171856 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172050 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "8cbffe56-0a93-59c5-9ea8-c4040e07bb03" :question/math-academy-id "e-8682" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are connected?\n\n![](images/ef/ef9e1dfd559c1e8818f14e100e07ab36ca167a4bd2ddf970bf3f5ef325103d64.png)" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, only regions I, II, and III satisfy this definition.\n\nRegion IV does not satisfy this definition. Note that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](images/d4/d4d61cf87f2c62c5cf4727384d6dfcc05cada6b23025dd6dd674130eaf64dd45.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171857 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/id #uuid "053b6396-341c-5b1f-a942-ca1fbf6efa7a" :question/math-academy-id "e-8684" :question/problem "Which of the regions shown below are simply connected?\n\n![](images/b8/b8e630b749cbfee41d73a620ffd284f3216bb8a43affdc26543f1eb57e4613c5.png)" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the regions: \n\n- Region I is not simply connected. Instead, this is a connected region that contains a hole.\n\n- Region II is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\n- Region III is not simply connected. Instead, this is a region that consists of two pieces (it's not connected).\n\n- Region IV is simply connected. This is a connected region that does not contain holes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171897 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/id #uuid "fb87998f-3236-510b-94aa-7db80487d8c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-9498" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: y-x\\geq 0\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y) \\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: (x,y)\\neq (0,0)\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2 \\: | \\: x^2+y^2> 4\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y \\geq x.$ So, it's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not*  simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(0,0).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc $x^2+y^2 \\leq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172050 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bce539c-19ae-54e9-9199-a573ddfc5136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6f/6f459a98398e9327b232f734b2e819798d3dcc6d66354edcd7d350aea8443a57.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487651} {:answer/id #uuid "42652284-7f15-59fe-b549-1dd2fe492f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cb/cb0e50751bed01a413a8417758c82a64aea7c5bf3a9a508347945bcb9681b01f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487698} {:answer/id #uuid "aac1dbad-2a8f-5c29-9358-0a80b2c2688f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d7d916e62541ad8d41f6043c0d0e2f511f0b79d036f6fce6b4ce4500a357023.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487895} {:answer/id #uuid "fdbc8357-c53c-5b1e-8b1c-081514832abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c43091934c162f690449769be8fa381b1ce5bcab3502883e56e4814fd4ace65a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488042} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf54361-0177-516c-b53c-a71ef9d79220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/61/6116e0dbea0e25ca27ea3ebd23356b0dd3d4ded0c2baf1ad4410f786f7b7bc6f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac1dbad-2a8f-5c29-9358-0a80b2c2688f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d7d916e62541ad8d41f6043c0d0e2f511f0b79d036f6fce6b4ce4500a357023.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487895} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd48dad3-3dbe-579f-a0a5-0256757f62c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488146}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "244776d4-c112-511f-a089-aa2567ad8e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-123880" :question/problem "Which of the following regions is connected?" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that satisfies this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/4d/4d7d916e62541ad8d41f6043c0d0e2f511f0b79d036f6fce6b4ce4500a357023.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259573 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172050 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d15f8fa8-f265-50da-b172-3ccb90895448" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fd295e1-1f3f-51b0-a531-01895286cbb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/ae77eaad51b8cd6bff4e62032946254da948e7643b45bd5e3a2343462ac457cb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257203} {:answer/id #uuid "7d496aba-750d-5723-bcf6-4b18fd5ca5ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257888} {:answer/id #uuid "a6346f12-fe1a-52b3-ae64-8730d965aa8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/98/98a0e2e2cd960a8065d83ce53336a727709d0228d43e28d3aed216f755aaafaa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258231} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d4af53-2db6-53e6-a9dc-bf20307ab33f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6c5f1576f6882e6e72633e7eb707f77d2707e0afa76307403848a58a8f45689a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258349} {:answer/id #uuid "b9912de7-1c35-55de-a866-f90635b99433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/27/2725284d21ba0b2514e5043ce1f776338e0480e0bb50c26234fae0a7d12d404c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d496aba-750d-5723-bcf6-4b18fd5ca5ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257888} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb37ec1-d922-5b73-967a-f71d5b47a3a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "856afbeb-9f59-56e5-affb-452bd8050ce2" :question/math-academy-id "q-123882" :question/problem "Which of the following regions is *not* connected?" :question/worked-solution "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n![](images/10/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png)\n\n \n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](images/2b/2bcaaf15d709d6396155bcdc9e8976bb037c9f341fc0b8863687958dbb0f40ff.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1af47ea-6253-5d58-9b94-31e52de27106" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a04266f-fa97-5bc9-a110-7f2c8e8f9f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/ba9b18a202db25c02b0907665d24fca75c9f4afc5babe898ff8f9c0227c7d447.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257297} {:answer/id #uuid "57b08ac5-e8a1-54f3-9c10-b1e40e64ae98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/82a33d59ae0060b0f1187415698ccf36ae45bd4ddc1fce0af74d01df74356ee1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257541} {:answer/id #uuid "88567626-0735-5cdd-944f-a824128be66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4a67c845fe7993fe0c91784c92201db6ff5c15098db04dc588f5ebe0e8cdc1a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257976} {:answer/id #uuid "89a42e11-a04d-52d9-9365-3edce26079d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28105671ce0984f8a34da01d06dc8251244073ced9f775fbc3ede8d9f63bea21.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257991} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ce7c6c-439b-564f-a3e1-577034a5bf56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d65f2e514477e8c935ddcf648f3073157489b083f1d108a81951e0499586f1c0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88567626-0735-5cdd-944f-a824128be66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4a67c845fe7993fe0c91784c92201db6ff5c15098db04dc588f5ebe0e8cdc1a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257976} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fb0f505-ea0d-5b4a-870d-b29b53c3b55d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de4d0c85-6915-5695-9beb-a379a8504775" :question/math-academy-id "q-123885" :question/problem "Which of the following is *not* a simply connected region?" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/46/46305c070e2563b4dacf8b31c88c46b860f003b20ffdff608a5485c09a91bd11.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/a0/a0459ddbabbd810e43db084f5dd174437340914b53ed227f6ef7ce2e3a0fc383.png)\n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following: \n\n![](images/4a/4a67c845fe7993fe0c91784c92201db6ff5c15098db04dc588f5ebe0e8cdc1a1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aec1b3a-f253-5279-99f6-12a688430707" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168610} {:answer/id #uuid "acbd015f-0d6c-538b-9f05-45ee71f8c513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168611} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e6ebd5-405c-535f-9ceb-b01c692d8bcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168612} {:answer/id #uuid "53f9ce92-f40b-51c9-86f1-dceb0bbaeb93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168613} {:answer/id #uuid "76624ec5-45cd-5b6f-a504-2ff12623de24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53f9ce92-f40b-51c9-86f1-dceb0bbaeb93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168613} :answer-field/id #uuid "2431be4b-89af-5247-a309-422a67c531ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8379be09-e532-538d-bf76-16e36177bb9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123890" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (1,1)\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,2x-y\\ne 0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(1,1).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=2x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab02e9fa-a18a-5bfa-9a4a-7874d2595d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462127} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3e1362-a334-597f-8485-f598c327597d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc3e1362-a334-597f-8485-f598c327597d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462128} :answer-field/id #uuid "21c918c9-a056-5a14-b108-cf36eee94f94" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0820282f-a984-584d-bb09-4ba91b706ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462129} {:answer/id #uuid "022346a4-c6ef-5e3d-be52-9a15682c2b6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0820282f-a984-584d-bb09-4ba91b706ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462129} :answer-field/id #uuid "40de5a38-0a97-54ce-bf6a-9b61bdad89f0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb50d634-93dd-5dba-aa37-be77a33be6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462131} {:answer/id #uuid "b52fb96c-4878-59cc-b25e-fe43a2f31ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb50d634-93dd-5dba-aa37-be77a33be6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462131} :answer-field/id #uuid "58585584-2f73-5c3c-ae4c-6fbf764850ac" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "beac61f6-0d9e-58bf-85d2-405f0693eb4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-123916" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (2,1)}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>25}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn. \n\n- Region I is simply connected. It's a plane region (a circle) without holes.\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole at $(2,1).$\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole. In this case, the hole contains all points on the disc ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 25.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488225 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c71b83-4367-5691-97de-b0703bcb7dd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487619} {:answer/id #uuid "45122bac-b3b8-5e27-afee-d630a49ce537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487702} {:answer/id #uuid "ce3274e2-524f-5cf1-9465-3aafe1e0f1a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487963} {:answer/id #uuid "f527e70a-5ed7-53da-91f5-358e6a505020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488026} {:answer/id #uuid "f7489938-f03a-5f2b-b530-6e9e1bed624b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45122bac-b3b8-5e27-afee-d630a49ce537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487702} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd56075-39b7-59a8-b93d-bcfc68b83760" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7361f82f-c91c-52b9-80ec-852a74fe03bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124773" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n\nI. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+2x\\ge 1\\}$\n\nII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-2x\\ne 1\\}$" :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge -2x+1.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region II is simply connected.  It's a plane region (a circle) without holes.\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=2x+1.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidian Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecde6e98-53fd-5ddd-bdc1-6ff205d00d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462139} {:answer/id #uuid "f49d1e0e-f360-53d6-9140-755bc53425ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f49d1e0e-f360-53d6-9140-755bc53425ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462140} :answer-field/id #uuid "a82752cf-bf54-5079-8c9f-a8fa8464cd75" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17fa137d-526a-57e9-8c8d-806b8a6e7139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462141} {:answer/id #uuid "482d1113-1761-5039-8696-fb7a9c674eea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17fa137d-526a-57e9-8c8d-806b8a6e7139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462141} :answer-field/id #uuid "62c5e294-13bc-5717-9f9c-3fef7f5d4399" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462824} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6953b99-2176-55bb-9f0e-69ab32d7d93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462143} {:answer/id #uuid "b13b7134-2fe3-59e1-90c8-cc035011e284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6953b99-2176-55bb-9f0e-69ab32d7d93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462143} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df54704-5657-56ec-913b-dbeb0cf13cfe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "387d1688-e72e-5fdc-bd02-55d9c19c099b" :question/math-academy-id "q-124775" :question/problem "Which of the following regions are simply connected?\n- **I.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y-x\\ge 0}$\n- **II.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>1}$\n- **III.** ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y+x\\ne 0}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A connected region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ can be contracted to a point.\n\n![](images/7d/7d6aea1a62fb290702630ef95ec86f4119e7c8fdd74b8148b62b66e5ac871b58.png)\n\nA connected *plane* region $D$ is simply connected if every simple closed curve in $D$ encloses only points in $D.$ In other words, the region does not contain any holes. Plane regions containing holes are not simply connected, since some simple closed curves cannot be contracted to a point:\n\n![](images/c3/c3c3e7a60ff0dd917cf6c0b293dae7510e457a0455629add1c54cadac65248b7.png)\n\nLet's now examine our regions in turn.\n\n- Region I is simply connected. Indeed, it is the half-plane $y\\ge x.$ So,   it's a plane region without holes,\n\n- Region II is *not* simply connected since it's a plane region with a hole (containing all points of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1$).\n\n- Region III is *not* simply connected. The region contains all the points of ${R}^{2}$ except those on the straight line $y=-x.$ Thus, the region is formed by two disjoint half-planes and, therefore, is not even a connected region.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "280e7ba4-7617-546b-9e0d-a5bdc33dad8d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Simply-Connected Regions in Euclidia